# Graphify knowledge graph outputs — collapse diffs in GitHub PR view
graphify-out/** linguist-generated=true

# The portfolio-import mirror and its sync script must stay LF on every platform.
#
# Two things break when git rewrites these to CRLF on a Windows checkout, and both
# are silent on CI, which runs on Linux and therefore never sees CRLF:
#
#   1. Vite cannot parse a CRLF .mjs. `functionsMirror.test.js` imports the sync
#      script for its file list, and the whole suite fails to collect with
#      "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" pointing at the import line.
#      `node --check` and esbuild both parse the same file happily, so the error
#      does not reproduce outside vitest and reads as a mystery.
#   2. The mirror is asserted BYTE-FOR-BYTE against src/. Line endings are bytes.
#      A generated file written with LF and checked out as CRLF is a permanent
#      false positive in `git status` and a false failure in the drift gate.
#
# Observed 2026-09-18, on the first Windows checkout after #951 merged.
scripts/build/*.mjs text eol=lf
functions/portfolioImport/esm/** text eol=lf
# The mirror is byte-compared against these, so both sides must agree on endings.
src/lib/portfolioImport/*.js text eol=lf
